"""HTTP routes over the capability handlers.

One route per capability -- POST creates the record, GET lists the caller's
records and GET /v1/<capability>/{id} reads one -- plus the operator surfaces
(discovery, the dashboard block's widgets, the formula catalogue, retrieval over
the co-op's own records, and the kernel roster).

Every route that touches tenant data takes its tenant from the authenticated
principal through ``require_platform_token``; no route reads a tenant from a
payload or a query string. A payload is validated at the edge with the
structured rejection the suite reads (which field, why, and the accepted
values), and a capability that refuses persists nothing: the ROUTE saves the
request through the tenant-scoped store, and only when the handler answered
``ok``.
"""

